tive Artificial Intelligence as a Tool for Teaching Communication in Nutrition and Dietetics Education—A Novel Education Innovation#🔴 Bulgular (Kırmızı)":[35,37],"#Generative Artificial Intelligence as a Tool for Teaching Communication in Nutrition and Dietetics Education—A Novel Education Innovation#🔴 Bulgular (Kırmızı)#{1}":[36,37],"#Generative Artificial Intelligence as a Tool for Teaching Communication in Nutrition and Dietetics Education—A Novel Education Innovation#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)":[38,40],"#Generative Artificial Intelligence as a Tool for Teaching Communication in Nutrition and Dietetics Education—A Novel Education Innovation#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)#{1}":[39,40],"#Generative Artificial Intelligence as a Tool for Teaching Communication in Nutrition and Dietetics Education—A Novel Education Innovation#🟠 Limitasyonlar (Turuncu)":[41,42]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Görüntüle","target":"zotero://select/library/items/X6EF293E","line":22},{"title":"14\" ([Sayfa 2","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/QICHEPZB?page=2&annotation=FCL4IUCE","line":30},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/QICHEPZB?page=1&annotation=BL7SAAKQ","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 3","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/QICHEPZB?page=3&annotation=UWG7U6M8","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/QICHEPZB?page=1&annotation=MH5AT4HZ","line":36},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/QICHEPZB?page=1&annotation=A3J2B7BM","line":39},{"title":"Sayfa 6","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/QICHEPZB?page=6&annotation=Z6X3H5SE","line":39}],"metadata":{"Title":"Generative Artificial Intelligence as a Tool for Teaching Communication in Nutrition and Dietetics Education—A Novel Education Innovation","Authors":"Lisa Barker, Joel Moore, Helmy Cook","Year":2024,"DOI":"10.3390/nu16070914","Nitelik":null,"Alan":null,"Konu":null,"AI_Methodology":null,"Layer_Focus":null,"Model_Asamasi":null,"Proposed_Tool":null,"Methods":"Presented here is a platform the authors have created that allows students to interact with virtual simulated patients to practise and develop their communication skills. Leveraging the structured incorporation of large language models, it is designed by pedagogical content experts and comprises individual cases based on curricula and student needsThe ATLAS platform allows pedagogical content experts to design individual cases based on curricula and student needs.The ATLAS platform allows pedagogical content experts to design individual cases based on curricula and student needs","Findings":"learning. Students appreciate the individualised and immediate feedback based on validated communication tools that encourage self-reflection and improvement.","Conclusions":"This platform harnesses the power of artificial intelligence to bridge the gap between theory and practice in communication skills training, requiring significantly reduced costs and resources than traditional simulated patient encounters.The use of AI to support nutrition and dietetic students’ healthcare communication is a new area in communication skills curricula. The uniquely developed ATLAS platform has many key strengths in its design, and its incorporation into the curriculum in a scaffolded manner allows for enhanced communication skill practice and greater educator and learner flexibility. Its adaptability means interdisciplinary application beyond nutrition and dietetics is straightforward. This platform not only bridges the gap between theory and practice in communication skills training, but also the gap between generative AI, academics and experienced practitioners.","Limitations":"","User_Notes":""},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"last_embed":{"hash":"qq23xu","at":1774939764075},"key":"Augmented Dietitian/barkerGenerativeArtificialIntelligence2024d.md"},
